    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Join our Discord to follow development and leave feedback! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is currently under development by Nicolas Nadeau (with help from RYRY77 early in development)  as of June 21st 2023 on the Unity engine. Myth of the Moirai is a third-person ARPG with influences from Diablo, Vampire Survivors, Final Fantasy, Dungeons &amp; Dragons, Rimworld,\u00a0 and Elder Scrolls.<br><br>Myth of The Moirai started as a single player game but I soon realized that multiplayer was a must for the game that I wanted to play. Now with full multiplayer and join on friends capabilities, you can explore the world with friends.<br><br>The game has gone through major content and graphical changes since its inception and first reveal almost 2 years ago now, and the game now runs on the latest version of Unity 6.<br><br>The first version of Myth Of The Moirai will feature a handmade dungeon with replayability through ever increasing difficulty and reward. Just talk to the Dark Messenger to increase the area level of the dungeon, unlock new areas, light up your path, upgrade your character, and much more.<br><br>Bring your friends in by using steams built in &quot;join on friend&quot; feature. Kill monsters together or duke it out in a duel to see who is stronger. You can even trade gear with eachother (currently just by dropping items on the ground).<br><br>In the future I plan on expanding the world to a central hub that will connect to multiple dungeons and a plot of land that you can build on and call your home. Make your home nice enough to entice NPC to join you to trade with and work for you.<br><br>Join our discord if you are interested in more information about the upcoming Alpha 0.00.01</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Join our Discord to follow development and leave feedback! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is currently under development by Nicolas Nadeau (with help from RYRY77 early in development)  as of June 21st 2023 on the Unity engine. Myth of the Moirai is a third-person ARPG with influences from Diablo, Vampire Survivors, Final Fantasy, Dungeons &amp; Dragons, Rimworld,\u00a0 and Elder Scrolls.<br><br>Myth of The Moirai started as a single player game but I soon realized that multiplayer was a must for the game that I wanted to play. Now with full multiplayer and join on friends capabilities, you can explore the world with friends.<br><br>The game has gone through major content and graphical changes since its inception and first reveal almost 2 years ago now, and the game now runs on the latest version of Unity 6.<br><br>The first version of Myth Of The Moirai will feature a handmade dungeon with replayability through ever increasing difficulty and reward. Just talk to the Dark Messenger to increase the area level of the dungeon, unlock new areas, light up your path, upgrade your character, and much more.<br><br>Bring your friends in by using steams built in &quot;join on friend&quot; feature. Kill monsters together or duke it out in a duel to see who is stronger. You can even trade gear with eachother (currently just by dropping items on the ground).<br><br>In the future I plan on expanding the world to a central hub that will connect to multiple dungeons and a plot of land that you can build on and call your home. Make your home nice enough to entice NPC to join you to trade with and work for you.<br><br>Join our discord if you are interested in more information about the upcoming Alpha 0.00.01</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
